Bundled third-party sources
---------------------------

src/vendor/vectorscan/

  Vectorscan 5.4.13, https://github.com/VectorCamp/vectorscan
  Copyright (c) 2015, Intel Corporation (Hyperscan)
  Copyright (c) 2020, VectorCamp PC
  Copyright (c) 2021, Arm Limited
  BSD-3-Clause licence; the full text ships alongside the sources as
  src/vendor/vectorscan/LICENSE and src/vendor/vectorscan/COPYING.

  The tree is the upstream release archive trimmed to what is needed to
  build libhs (tools/vendor/keep/vectorscan.txt), with these local
  patches applied by tools/vendor/fetch from tools/patches/vectorscan/:

    0001-ragel-optional.patch             build without Ragel from the
                                          pre-generated parser sources
    0002-fat-runtime-hs-flags.patch       apply -Wno-error to the x86-64
                                          fat runtime build
    0003-build-wrapper-without-rev.patch  fat-runtime symbol prefixing
                                          without rev(1)
    0004-drop-diagnostic-pragmas.patch    remove the pragmas R CMD check
                                          notes
    0005-build-wrapper-rename-asan-odr-indicators.patch
                                          fat-runtime symbol prefixing also
                                          renames AddressSanitizer ODR
                                          indicators

  The patches carry the same licence as the files they change.

  Within that tree, src/vendor/vectorscan/LICENSE also covers:

  - Intel's Slicing-by-8 CRC32 implementation,
    Copyright (c) 2004-2006, Intel Corporation, BSD licence.
  - Patched Boost Graph headers under
    src/vendor/vectorscan/include/boost-patched/, Boost Software
    License 1.0.

Boost headers used at build time come from the BH package and are not
bundled.

The regex parser sources src/vendor/vectorscan/src/parser/*.rl.cpp are
generated by Ragel (tools/vendor/fetch) from the bundled .rl files and carry
the same copyright and licence as those files.

No other third-party code is included.
